{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["<b>And the land shall be left desolate by them, and shall enjoy its sabbaths.</b> For at first it had been demanding redress for its shame and the nullification of its sabbatical years, and after justice was done upon the sinners — then 'the land shall be left desolate by them' and shall no longer complain about the nullification of its sabbaths. 'And it shall enjoy' — that is, it will be appeased by the matter."], :book :leviticus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:38:52.492486602Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}